From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: admit shared-memory widgets and defer unavailable Uke amps

The strict widget callback exposes the buffer loader's missing shared-memory
endpoint cases. Both endpoints need common module parsing but have no hardware
interface tokens. Accept them without suppressing unknown-module or parser errors.

An amplifier that NACKs at boot must not become a permanently disabled component.
Defer transient bus failures so driver-core supplier progress can retry detection.
Keep reset asserted, reject unsupported chip families and retain preset, gain,
PLL and thermal gates. No calibration or persistent device data is changed.

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/fs19xx.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/fs19xx.c
@@ -988,8 +988,10 @@
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL, "reset-gpios must be GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW\n");
 
 	ret = fs19xx_detect(fs19xx, &chipid);
-	if (ret == -EPROBE_DEFER)
-		return ret;
+	if (ret == -EPROBE_DEFER || ret == -ENXIO || ret == -EAGAIN ||
+	    ret == -ETIMEDOUT)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
+				     "amplifier bus not ready\n");
 	if (ret) {
 		/*
 		 * Keep the component so the sound card (and HDMI) still binds; this
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/topology.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/topology.c
@@ -963,6 +963,10 @@
 	mod_array = audioreach_get_module_array(&tplg_w->priv);
 
 	switch (mod->module_id) {
+	case MODULE_ID_WR_SHARED_MEM_EP:
+	case MODULE_ID_RD_SHARED_MEM_EP:
+		/* Shared-memory endpoints have no hardware-interface tokens. */
+		break;
 	case MODULE_ID_CODEC_DMA_SINK:
 	case MODULE_ID_CODEC_DMA_SOURCE:
 		audioreach_widget_dma_module_load(mod, mod_array);
